          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %strong inverse semigroup
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (ie. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
            %em unique
            “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"}> inverse
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^*\in S
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s s^* s = s
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^* s s^* = s^*
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{\ast\ast} = s
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Needless to say, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            is an inverse semigroup. More to the point however:
          %ul
            %li
              The fundamental example is the following: for any set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(X)
              be the set of all partial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
              (or as
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+functions"} partial functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(X)
              by the “Cayley’s theorem” for inverse semigroups (see below).
          %p
            This inverse semigroup plays a role in the theory similar to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
            groups in the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
          %blockquote
            %p Groups describe global symmetries, while inverse semigroups describe local symmetries.
          %p Other examples include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a topological space, let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)\subseteq I(X)
                consist of the homeomorphisms between open subsets of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudogroup+of+transformations"} pseudogroup of transformations
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (a general pseudogroup of transformations is a sub-inverse-semigroup of
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet-semilattice"} meet-semilattice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is an inverse semigroup under the meet operation.
            %li
              %p
                Exel’s inverse semigroup
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(G)
                of a finite group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Exel95"} Exel 95
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(G)
                to
                %em partial
                representations of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h2#properties Properties
          .query
            %p
              Lots to say here: the meet-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotents"} idempotents
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+groupoid"} ordered groupoid
          %h3#idempotents_form_a_subsemigroup Idempotents form a subsemigroup
          #triv.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in an inverse semigroup,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x^\ast
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast x
              are idempotent. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is idempotent, then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^\ast = e
          %p The proof is trivial.
          #comm.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In an inverse semigroup, the product of any two idempotents
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e, f
              is idempotent, and any two idempotents commute.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              One easily checks that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e f)^\ast = f(e f)^\ast e
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(e f)^\ast e
              is an idempotent. So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e f)^\ast
              is idempotent; as a result,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e f)^\ast = e f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e f
              and similarly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e
              are idempotent. Next we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e f (f e) e f = e f^2 e^2 f = e f e f = e f, \qquad f e (e f) f e = f e^2 f^2 e = f e f e = f e
            %p
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e, f, e f, f e
              are all idempotent, and so
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi e
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi e
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e = (e f)^\ast = e f
          %p
            Thus the idempotents in an inverse semigroup form a subsemigroup which is commutative and idempotent. Such a structure is the same as a meet-semilattice except for the fact that there might not have an empty meet or top element; that is, we define an order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            on idempotents by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \leq f
            if and only if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = e f
          %h3#_is_an_antiinvolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            is an anti-involution
          #invol.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              For any two elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              in an inverse semigroup,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x y)^\ast = y^\ast x^\ast
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since the idempotents
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast x, y y^\ast
              commute, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y (y^\ast x^\ast) x y = x (y y^\ast)(x^\ast x) y = x x^\ast x y y^\ast y = x y
            %p
              and similarly
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y^\ast x^\ast (x y)y^\ast x^\ast = y^\ast y y^\ast x^\ast x x^\ast = y^\ast x^\ast
          %h3#order_structure Order structure
          #ord.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              in an inverse semigroup, the following are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                There exists an idempotent
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi e
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = e y
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x x^\ast y
                ,
              %li
                There exists an idempotent
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y f
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y x^\ast x
                \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We show
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo .
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 2
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3. \Rightarrow 2.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 4
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1. \Rightarrow 4.
              Clearly then we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 2
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 1
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 4
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 3
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3. \Rightarrow 2. \Rightarrow 1. \Rightarrow 4. \Rightarrow 3.
            %p
              Given an idempotent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %msup
                              %mi y
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                            %msup
                              %mi y
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mi since
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi idempotents
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi commute
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                            %mi f
                            %msup
                              %mi y
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi y
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mtext Proposition 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mi f
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mtext Lemma 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mo *
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp; = &amp; y f &amp; \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; y y^\ast y f &amp; \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; y f y^\ast y &amp; since \; idempotents \; commute \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; y f f y^\ast y &amp; \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; y f f^\ast y^\ast y &amp; \text{Proposition 1} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; y f (y f)^\ast y &amp; \text{Lemma 2} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; x x^\ast y &amp;
                    }
            %p
              which gives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mo .
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mn 2
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3. \Rightarrow 2.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            is defined on an inverse semigroup by saying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
            if any of the four conditions of Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ord"}
            is satisfied; transitivity follows by equivalence to 1. and closure of idempotents under multiplication. When restricted to idempotents, this preorder coincides with the meet-semilattice order.
          #order.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq b
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
              in an inverse semigroup, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x \leq b y
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≤
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast \leq y^\ast
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Writing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = e b
              for some idempotent
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x = e (b x)
              and so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi b
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x \leq b x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi b
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b x \leq b y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x \leq b y
              by transitivity. This gives
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi b
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x \leq b y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = e y
              for an idempotent
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast = (e y)^\ast = y^\ast e^\ast
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≤
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast \leq y^\ast
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
              on an inverse semigroup is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq x
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              From
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
              we derive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast \leq y^\ast
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x^\ast \leq y y^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq x
              we derive
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y y^\ast \leq x x^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x^\ast = y y^\ast
              since the preorder on idempotents is a meet-semilattice, which is a partial order. Then from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
              we derive
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mo *
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x x^\ast y = y y^\ast y = y
          %p
            Thus an inverse semigroup is naturally regarded as an internal semigroup in the category of posets (equivalently, a finite-product preserving functor from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            of semigroups to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
          %h3#RelationToOrderedGroupoids Relation to ordered groupoids
          %p
            In this section, an
            %em ordered groupoid
            means an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            of posets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi SemiCat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd(C) \to SemiCat(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicategory"} semicategory
            (remembering only composition of morphisms, forgetting presence of inverses and identity morphisms), has a right adjoint which takes a semicategory to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            groupoid of the category of idempotents attached to a semicategory (see
            %a{:href => "/nlab/show/semicategory#idempotents"} here
            for details). (This observation is formulated in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} finite limit logic
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Set
          %p
            In particular, this construction may be applied to an inverse semigroup seen as a semigroup in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(S)
              attached to an inverse semigroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is the core of the category of idempotents
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Idem
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem(S)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
              is viewed as a one-object semicategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B S
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Pos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
          %p
            In more detail: an arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \to e'
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Idem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem(S)
            is a triple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e, x, e')
            of elements in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e, e'
            are idempotent elements and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is an element such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                    %mo ′
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x e = x = e' x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = x^\ast x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e' = x x^\ast
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: x^\ast x \to x x^\ast
          %p
            A key example to keep in mind is the inverse semigroup of partial bijections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            on a set, where the arrows of the corresponding groupoid are actual invertible maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi range
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dom(\phi) \to range(\phi)
            between subsets. In general, the object part of the associated groupoid is not just a poset, but a poset with binary meets.
          %p
            The reason for the notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(S)
            is that this ordered groupoid is a so-called
            = succeed "," do
              %em inductive groupoid
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong inductive groupoid
              is an internal groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
              with the following additional properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The object part
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
                  admits binary meets;
              %li
                %p
                  Given
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: e \to f
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e' \leq e
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo :
                        %mi e
                        %mo ′
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x': e' \to f
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
                  with
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \leq x
                  %em restriction
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo *
                          %mi e
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x|_\ast e']
              %li
                %p
                  Given
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: e \to f
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \geq f'
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo :
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x': e \to f'
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
                  with
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≥
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \geq x'
                  %em corestriction
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo ′
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f' _\ast| x]
          %p
            In fact conditions 2. and 3. in this definition are equivalent. A
            %em morphism
            of inductive groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to G'
            is an internal functor from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G'
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an inductive groupoid, a tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes: G_1 \times G_1 \to G_1
            may be defined by the rule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo *
                  %mi dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi cod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi cod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes y = [x|_\ast dom(x) \wedge cod(y)] \cdot [dom(x) \wedge cod(y) _\ast|y]
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
            indicates composition in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_1, \otimes)
            is an inverse semigroup
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Inv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Inv(G)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Ehresmann-Schein-Nampooripad)
              There are canonical isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi Inv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to Inv(Ind(S))
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ind
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Inv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to Ind(Inv(G))
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi InvSemiGrp
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi IndGpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} InvSemiGrp \simeq IndGpd
          %h3#warning_on_the_definition Warning on the definition
          %p With only a subtle change in definition, the result is that one gets only groups:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              semigroup with the property that for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
              there exists a unique
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a x a = a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a group.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is inhabited, say by an element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b b^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x e = x
              for any
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e x = x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is an identity (
              %em the
              identity
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a a^\ast
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^\ast a
              equal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a group.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a y a = a
              for unique
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a y a) y a = a y a = a
              it follows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mi a
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y a y = y
              and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is an inverse semigroup. The same observation means it is enough to show
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x e) x^\ast (x e) = x e
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\ast (x e) x^\ast = x^\ast
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi e
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x e = x
            %p The above results on inverse semigroups apply and we derive
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mo *
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                            %mi e
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mo *
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mo *
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                          %mtd
                            %mi Proposition
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                          %mtd
                            %mi Lemma
                            %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x e x^\ast x e &amp; = &amp; x e e x^\ast x e &amp; \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; x e e^\ast x^\ast x e &amp; Proposition \; 1 \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; x e (x e)^\ast x e &amp; Lemma 2 \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; x e
                    }
            %p as was to be shown.
          %h3#wagnerpreston_theorem_cayleys_theorem_for_inverse_semigroups
            %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverse_semigroup#Homomorphisms_and_representations_of_inverse_semigroups"}> Wagner-Preston Theorem
            \: “Cayley’s Theorem” for inverse semigroups
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Every inverse semigroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              can be realized as a semigroup of partial bijections on a set.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              First use the conventional Cayley’s theorem to embed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{End}(S)
              through the map sending
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
              to the map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi sx
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\mapsto sx
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mtext End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{End}(S)
            %p
              For each map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\ast s s^\ast=s^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{s^\ast(S)}:s^\ast(S)\rightarrow s(S)
              has left inverse
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\ast|_{s(S)}:s(S)\rightarrow s^\ast(S)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s s^\ast s=s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{s^\ast(S)}
              is a bijection.
            %p
              Consider the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\rightarrow I(S)
              defined by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\mapsto (s|_{s^\ast(S)}: s^\ast(S)\rightarrow s(S))
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t\in S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{s^\ast(S)}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t|_{t^\ast(S)}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(S)\cap t^\ast (S)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t|_{t^\ast(S)}\circ s|_{s^\ast(S)}
              is then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ts
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\ast (s(S)\cap t^\ast (S))=s^\ast t^\ast(S)=(ts)^\ast (S)
              as required. Finally, we check injectivity. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t\in S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_{s^\ast(S)}=t_{t^\ast(S)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\ast(S)=t^\ast(S)
              so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ss
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ts
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ss^\ast=ts^\ast
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi s
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi t
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^\ast s s^\ast = s^\ast t s^\ast
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s=t
